        "Performance Features",
        "1. Large air intake and low energy consumption.\n2. Capable of self‑air‑suction and self‑pulp‑suction. Adopts horizontal layout, no froth pump is required for middling return.\n3. Low impeller peripheral speed and long service life of wearing parts.\n4. There is a relatively large clearance between impeller and cover plate (also known as stator). The clearance enlargement caused by wear has little impact on air intake.\n5. The pulp inside the cell follows a fixed flow pattern to realize vertical double‑circulation, which facilitates the suspension of coarse‑grained minerals.",
        "",
